{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 view limit, answer to ed041dcc. The per-view limit of 16 stays. Sorting the state lists is fine, because it changes order and not values.\n1. First choice, as you propose: keep the explicit state and every primary publication and retirement fact inline, and move the overflow to a linked details record. Do this only if current projection routing expresses the link with no new Native reference.\n2. If it cannot, use this display priority, from first to keep to first to move off the card:\n   (a) state, and what the member can do next\n   (b) the event's own title and time\n   (c) the publication outcome and the retirement fact\n   (d) who acted\n   (e) provenance and identifiers: digests, source references, internal numbers\n   Move the lowest-ranked fact off the card. It stays in the record, in the witness assertions and in explain output, so nothing becomes unreadable.\nIn the review request, list all 17 facts with their rank, name the one that moved, and say which option applied.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}